Hi, y'all nethaddicts;

I just ascended a samurai (my second 3.1 ascension; first one was priest),
and I noticed something in both games that I would like yo hear your
comments on.

Warning, possible spoilers:

^L














In both games, after grabbing the amulet from the Sanctum, I had a *LOT* of
difficulty coming back out of Gehennom. About 2 out of 3 times trying to
go upstairs from any given level, I would get some message (I forget the
exact wording, but it said something to the effect that I was temporarily
disoriented), and end up on a deeper level instead of a shallower one, 
sometimes even three or four levels deeper. This became very annoying after
a while, especially since on many levels it isn't possible to teleport.
Does anyone know what causes this, or if there is any way around
it? I presume the Amulet is responsible, but could it be the combination
of carrying the Amulet and something else? It took me several hours to
get back from level 54 to level 30 or so (where Gehennom started). A very
frustrating experience. Is the only remedy sheer obstinacy? Once I left
Gehennom, it didn't happen anymore.

On another line of thought, someone recently posted a number of hints and
spoilers about endgame strategy. One thing mentioned it that on the elemental 
levels the portal can be *anywhere*. I don't think this is true. On the earth
level, I think the portal has to be within one of the cavities initially
present on the level, on the air level I don't think the portal can be
in the clouds, on the fire level I don't think the portal can be in a pool
of lava, and on the water level the portal moves around inside one of the
air bubbles. By the way, no amulet of magical breathing is required to
survive outside the air bubbles. I don't know about the necessity of wearing
a ring of levitation (I was wearing one anyway). Finally I remember reading
some message about the astral level being somewhat anticlimactic, since it
was possible to directly teleport to the final altar to offer the Amulet.
This isn't possible for me. Teleporting is strictly impossible anywhere
on any of the 5 endgame levels. You have to hack your way through hordes
of Angels and Priests, plus a couple of nasty Demons. Has anyone tried to
eat the corpses left by Death, Famine or Pestilence? I didn't dare... Also,
are Death, Famine and Pestilence always associated with the chaotic, neutral
and lawful antechambers, respectively, as they were for me?

One item I picked up and wore until the end is an oilskin cloak. What does
it do? There was no difference in my intrinsics before and after wearing it,
and I got a "this cloak fits very tightly around your body" (or something
like that) message when I put it on. Is it supposed to prevent armor
worn underneath from rusting when immersed?

I eventually got tired of peaceful Orcus following me everywhere and getting
in my way, so I chopped him in to with my Tsurugi. I think this is what cost
me telepathy, but I had a helm of telepathy, so who cares? Is there any way
to get rid of such peaceful annoying demon lords without the chaotic approach?
Teleporting away didn't seem to work. Somehow Orcus seemed to love me too much.
Well, it IS Valentine's day after all...

Last thing, when I finally ascended, my spellbooks of magic mapping and
identify (both kept in an uncursed bag of holding) had turned to blanks,
but not my spellbook of finger of death. The bag hadn't become cursed at
any time, but I did fall in water a couple of times in Gehennom. Is that
what did it? (I thought bags of holding were absolutely safe storage places
except if they became cursed).

All right, this time I'm *REALLY* going back to my thesis.

